  "measurement_semantics": [
    "Only Ascend hardware events carrying Task Type are counted as device tasks; synthesized Computing/Free tracks, NOTIFY_WAIT wrappers, HostToDevice flows and CPU labels are not added to kernel durations.",
    "Device attention sums contain sequential KERNEL_MIX_AIC executions. Attention envelope includes gaps between those executions and is not pure kernel time.",
    "Between-attention gaps contain every task between attention executions; for per_layer they include real AICPU metadata computation, while legacy gaps are predominantly update waits. They are not universally idle-device time.",
    "MEM_WAIT_VALUE duration is a separate queue-wait diagnostic; NOTIFY_WAIT and host synchronization overlap device execution. Do not sum these with kernels into endpoint latency.",
    "Legacy npu::npu_fused_infer_attention_score CPU durations cover the replay-time update operator calls. Nested aclnn durations are included within those calls and must not be added. graph_task_update_begin/end are not separately timed by these names.",
    "Profile record_function labels enclose replay and synchronize, excluding prepare; they include profiler overhead and are not the formal wall endpoint.",
    "Formal queue_span_us includes possible host submission gaps, external waits and update-stream joins. Formal wall_us includes required mode-specific metadata preparation/H2D and final synchronization.",
    "attention_only has a freshly generated exact plan outside its timed interval; it is a diagnostic ceiling, not an executable dynamic algorithm without planning."
  ],
